<h1 id="extesttab-title" style="color:#0d47a1;font-size:1.5em;font-weight:700;border-bottom:2px solid #90caf9;padding-bottom:0.25em;margin-top:0"><code>extesttab</code> — expgtest run + scoreboard tables</h1>

**Type:** keyword campaign · **Not always-on** — mention **`extesttab`** or `@` this rule.  
**Owns:** (1) one or more live `expgtest` campaigns, (2) append to [`docs/pglpl/EXPGTEST_CATALOG_SCOREBOARD.md`](../../../docs/pglpl/EXPGTEST_CATALOG_SCOREBOARD.md) with **Ex-run** sequence numbers, (3) per-run **iteration breakdown** tables (mrkd HTML) including **Remaining scopes + words** when 1–4 scopes remain at iter start, (4) **pairwise** compare of the N runs in one session, (5) optional **triple compare** vs a named prior Ex-run, (6) freshman-plain summary in chat.  
**Does not own:** `pgbattest` / `pgtestcom`; git commit (`gitacp`).

## Document outline

1. [When this applies](#when) — trigger + parse.
2. [Locks / defaults](#locks) — frozen ambiguities.
3. [Procedure](#procedure) — run → parse → record → compare → reply.
4. [Scoreboard write shape](#scoreboard) — Ex-run sections + markers.
5. [Table columns](#tables) — iteration breakdown contract.
6. [Chat reply shape](#reply) — mandatory summary.
7. [Examples](#examples).
8. [Related rules](#related).

