<h2 id="reply" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">6. Chat reply shape</h2>

Mandatory **freshman-plain** summary:

<table>
<thead>
<tr style="background:#1565c0;color:white"><th>What happened</th><th>One-line result</th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td style="background:#e3f2fd">Ex-run ids assigned</td><td style="background:#e8f5e9">e.g. Ex-run 3 + Ex-run 4</td></tr>
<tr><td style="background:#e3f2fd">Scopes</td><td style="background:#e8f5e9">full-23 or named subset</td></tr>
<tr><td style="background:#e3f2fd">Pass / blocked</td><td style="background:#e8f5e9">e.g. 23/23 cleared vs blocked on 429</td></tr>
<tr><td style="background:#e3f2fd">Wall</td><td style="background:#fff8e1">seconds + ~minutes per run</td></tr>
<tr><td style="background:#e3f2fd">Scoreboard</td><td style="background:#fff8e1">Link to <code>docs/pglpl/EXPGTEST_CATALOG_SCOREBOARD.md#ex-run-N</code></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>

One sentence on pairwise (and baseline, if any). Do **not** dump full HTML tables in chat — point to scoreboard.

